      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looks OK to me. Again, haven\u0027t verified. It seems sensible though to remove CPUs which have a non-preemptible task right now from the set, and if we didn\u0027t find any we start again with the whole set.\n\nThe definition here of non-preemptible task is handling softIRQs, running softirqd or handling hard irqs, not tasks currently which interrupts disabled.\n\nWe\u0027re accepting the possibility that we displace a lower priority RT task in order to avoid the wakeup latency penalty if we hit something which can\u0027t be interrupted for a while.\n",
